<title>CHINA: China's Xinjiang sets grain, cotton output targets.</title>
<headline>China's Xinjiang sets grain, cotton output targets.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's northwestern region of Xinjiang has set a target to produce 8.0 million tonnes of grain and 1.15 million tonnes of cotton in 1997, the China news service said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cotton output in Kashgar was expected to be 270,000 tonnes this year while output in Aksu would be 200,000 tonnes, the report said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>Xinjiang, China's main cotton producing region, produced 1.0 million tonnes of cotton in 1996.</p>
<p>China's cotton output in 1996 was estimated at 4.0 million tonnes, down by 800,000 tonnes from the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
